# Line endings.
#
# The repository stores LF. Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true hands out
# CRLF working copies and Git has to guess on the way back in, which is how a one-line edit
# turns into a whole-file diff in review. `eol=lf` settles it for every text file: LF in the
# index, LF in the working tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Assets, where a newline conversion would silently corrupt the file.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary

# The post-mortem export is compared byte for byte in the tests, so it is not a place to be
# clever about normalisation either.
*.md text eol=lf
